# sprint_sec_ci_product.oot — SEC hostile audit of ci_product rails
# Date: 2026-08-14
# Role: SEC. This file only. No product edit. Did not touch ci_product.* / sh.oo.
# Marker: ci_product.oo twin present; ci_product_rails.oo ABSENT
# Surfaces: ooda/scripts/ci_product.sh (250 L), ooda/scripts/ci_product.oo (47 L),
#           ooda/std/sh.oo sh_arg_ok (L20-33), ooda/std/scenario.oo,
#           ooda/runtime/chs_rt_sys.c oo_sys_exec, ooda/scripts/bootstrap_no_cargo.sh,
#           ooda/scripts/sh_arg_ok_smoke.oo, .github/workflows/product.yml
# Method: static hunt. No live inject probe this turn. Do not claim secure.
# Hunt: rail-name command injection | PATH shadow holes | bootstrap + unsanitized env
# Honesty: product rail is still ci_product.sh (GHA + PM). The .oo is not a runner.

========================================================================
VERDICT
========================================================================

**Not secure. Not a replacement. Do not green the .oo twin.**

`ci_product.sh` is the live product rail. Rail names there are static
literals and quoted on exec. That path has **no** rail-name command
injection today.

`ci_product.oo` is a story that prints PASSED. It does not list or run
the 132 rails. `ci_product_rails.oo` is **absent** (HYG same wave).
Every `check` / `expect_*` Result is dropped. `when`/`and`/`then` are
empty. That is honesty fraud, not a seal.

The .oo **does** build one `sh -c` line that interpolates `seed`,
`shadow`, `tmpd`, and `root` with **no** `sh_arg_ok` at the concat
site. That is the new inject surface. `sh_arg_ok` would not close it:
the class allows space, `=`, `:`, `/`, `.`. Those are enough to
rewrite `SEED_OODAC=` / `PATH=` and to exec a second word.

PATH shadow is cargo/rustc only. It is not a PATH pin.
Bootstrap on the .sh path inherits the full parent env
(`BASH_ENV`, `LD_PRELOAD`, `IFS`, `OODA_SEED_ALLOW_UNSIGNED`,
`OODA_STD`). Minisign is `env -i`. The seed build is not.

Do not say the char gate makes ci_product safe.

========================================================================
SURFACES
========================================================================

| Surface | Path | Role |
|---------|------|------|
| Live rail | `ooda/scripts/ci_product.sh` | GHA `product.yml` + PM + residual echo |
| Twin | `ooda/scripts/ci_product.oo` | 47 L; no rail loop; unconditional PASSED |
| Split | `ooda/scripts/ci_product_rails.oo` | **ABSENT** |
| Arg gate | `ooda/std/sh.oo` L20-33 | whitelist; space `=` `:` `/` `.` `-` `+` `_` |
| Env read | `sh_env_get_or` L136-141 | `printenv KEY \|\| echo DEFAULT` via `sh -c` |
| Exec | `process_exec` → `sys_exec("sh","-c",cmd)` | no stdout (`chs_rt_sys.c:289-291`) |
| Child env | `oo_sys_exec` L245-283 | keep `OODA_*`/`OO_*`; pin `PATH=/usr/bin:/bin` |
| Seed build | `bootstrap_no_cargo.sh` | SHA+minisign; build is `env -u OODA` only |
| Gate smoke | `sh_arg_ok_smoke.oo` | `;` `&&` `$(` only. Not space. Not `=`. Not `../` |
| Compare | `install_dress_rehearsal.oo` | `dress_gate` = `sh_arg_ok` + exit. ci_product.oo has none |

========================================================================
HUNT 1 — command injection in rail names
========================================================================

`.sh` today: **no inject**. Rails are a static word list (L73-205).
132 names, all `[a-z0-9_]+\.sh`. Exec is quoted:

    "$ROOT/scripts/$rail" >"$TMPDIR/ci_$rail.out" 2>"$TMPDIR/ci_$rail.err"

Quotes make `;` `|` space one filename, not a second command.
IFS does not resplit literal words in the `for` list.
Rails are not read from env, argv, or a file.

Residual on the same lines (editor / future data, not today's list):

| Vector | Quoted exec | Still |
|--------|-------------|-------|
| `foo; id.sh` | one path | need that file to exist |
| `../evil` | one path | **YES** — `$ROOT/scripts/../evil` |
| `ci_$rail.out` with `/` in rail | one path | write under `$TMPDIR/ci_../…` |
| `chmod +x "$ROOT/scripts/$rail"` | one path | +x a traversal target if listed |
| empty rail | `"$ROOT/scripts/"` | exec a directory; fail |

`.oo` today: **no rail names at all**. Beat L21 says
"every listed rail exits 0". Nothing listed. Nothing run.
`ci_product_rails.oo` does not exist. A 132-rail loop cannot
fit in the 47-line twin and stay under the 256-line lock.
The split file was the place a `rail_ok` gate would live.
It is not there.

If a later twin does the obvious concat:

    check(p, root + "/scripts/" + rail + " > " + tmpd + "/ci_" + rail + ".out")

then rail names become part of `sh -c`. Today's literals would
survive. These would not, and `sh_arg_ok` would **allow** them:

| Rail / payload | `sh_arg_ok` | `sh -c` concat |
|----------------|-------------|----------------|
| `chs_parity.sh` | accept | fine (literal) |
| `foo bar.sh` | **accept** (space) | `> tmp/ci_foo` then cmd `bar.sh.out` |
| `x PATH=/tmp/e /tmp/e/pwn` | **accept** | second command + PATH rewrite |
| `../bootstrap/seed/oodac` | **accept** (`/` `.`) | path traversal, not meta |
| `-rf` | **accept** | option inject if used as argv |
| `foo;id` | reject | class works |
| `$(id)` / `` `id` `` | reject | class works |
| `foo&&bar` | reject (`&`) | class works |
| newline | reject | class works |
| `""` empty | **accept** (n=0 → true) | missing separator |

`sh_arg_ok` is the wrong gate for a rail leaf. A rail leaf needs
`[A-Za-z0-9_]+\.sh`, no `/`, no space, no leading `-`, bounded
length. Nobody wrote that function.

`sh_arg_ok_smoke.oo` does not test space, `=`, `:`, `../`,
leading `-`, empty, or newline. A green smoke is not this hunt.

`.sh` `chmod +x` on a missing-but-present file (L207-211) is not
inject. It is "make the listed path executable." Keep the list
static and quoted.

========================================================================
HUNT 2 — PATH shadow holes
========================================================================

Intended threat: refuse accidental `cargo` / `rustc`.
Not a threat they sealed: full PATH pin, `env` hijack, colon
split, `/usr/bin/cargo`.

`.sh` (L30-44, L62-68, then the rail loop):

    SHADOW="$TMPDIR/ci_product_shadow_$$"
    # only two files: cargo, rustc → exit 99
    export PATH="$SHADOW:$PATH"

Holes:

1. **Prepend, do not pin.** `find`, `grep`, `wc`, `chmod`, `mkdir`,
   `tail`, `sha256sum`, `gcc`, and `env` still come from the rest
   of PATH. L53 `find "$ROOT" -name '*.rs'` is attacker `find`
   if PATH was poisoned before entry.
2. **Rails use `#!/usr/bin/env bash`.** `env` is not in SHADOW.
   PATH=`SHADOW:/tmp/evil:/usr/bin` → `/tmp/evil/env` wins.
   That is a PATH-shadow hole on every rail.
3. **TMPDIR colon splits PATH.**
   `TMPDIR=/tmp/x:/tmp/evil` →
   `SHADOW=/tmp/x:/tmp/evil/ci_product_shadow_PID` →
   `PATH=/tmp/x:/tmp/evil/ci_product_shadow_PID:…`
   `/tmp/x` is searched first for `cargo`, `env`, `find`.
   `:` is not special-cased. `sh_arg_ok` would also allow `:`.
4. **Absolute cargo bypass.** `/usr/bin/cargo`,
   `~/.cargo/bin/cargo`, `rustup`. Hygiene grep (L21-28) only
   scans three scripts for a *bare* `cargo`/`rustc` line.
   Rails are not scanned. GHA has a separate workflow grep.
5. **Shadow lives under TMPDIR.** Default is relative
   `.ooda-cache/ooda-tmp`. World-writable + predictable `$$`
   is a local replace-after-chmod class. Not CI-fork RCE by
   itself. Do not call the dir a capability.
6. **Detection is log grep** (L237) for `ERR_SHADOW_*`.
   A rail that calls cargo by abs path never prints that
   string. FN.

GHA `product.yml` prepends its own shadow via `GITHUB_PATH`,
then `ci_product.sh` prepends another. Same shape. Same holes.
Runner image `env`/`find` still sit on PATH after the shadow.

`.oo` is a **different** PATH, not a tighter one:

- `oo_sys_exec` pins child `PATH=/usr/bin:/bin` (L283).
- Shadow files are written under `tmpd + "/ci_shadow"`.
- Only two commands prefix `PATH=` + shadow + `:/usr/bin:/bin`
  (L32-33 cargo probe, L41 bootstrap).
- `fixed_point.sh` (L43) has **no** shadow prefix. Child PATH
  is `/usr/bin:/bin`. **`/usr/bin/cargo` is live.**
- Future rails invoked the same way also see `/usr/bin/cargo`,
  not the shadow.
- L32 is `… cargo version … || true`. Always Ok. Not a test.
- L33 only proves intercept **when** PATH is prefixed.
  It does not prove the suite is under that PATH.

So the .oo "shadow" wraps two strings. It does not wrap the
product suite. Host `/usr/bin/cargo` is the PATH-shadow hole
the .sh at least tried to cover.

`expect_quiet` (scenario.oo L88-99) also checks stdout empty.
`oo_sys_exec` success is `oo_str_lit("")`. Stdout is never
returned. The empty-stdout half of expect_quiet is dead.
Exit status is the only signal.

========================================================================
HUNT 3 — bootstrap invoked with unsanitized env
========================================================================

`.sh` L62-63:

    SEED_OODAC="${SEED_OODAC:-$_SEED_DEFAULT}" "$ROOT/scripts/bootstrap_no_cargo.sh"

This is a **quoted prefix assignment**. The value is data, not
shell. `;` in SEED_OODAC does not inject here. Good.

The process is bash. The env is the **full parent env**.

| Var | Reaches bootstrap.sh? | Effect |
|-----|------------------------|--------|
| `BASH_ENV` / `ENV` | **YES** | sourced **before line 1** of ci_product.sh and again on the shebang bash of bootstrap. RCE at entry. Shadow does not exist yet. |
| `LD_PRELOAD` / `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` / `DYLD_*` | **YES** | seed ELF + gcc in L158-168. Minisign only is `env -i` (L136). |
| `IFS` | **YES** | word-split inside bootstrap / pure_build |
| `PATH` | shadow prepended | see hunt 2; not pinned |
| `TMPDIR` | exported L12 | seed copy path ` $TMPDIR/bootstrap_seed_oodac ` |
| `OODA_SEED_ALLOW_UNSIGNED=1` | **YES** | L99 skip minisign. Product-trust bypass. Loud WARN is not a seal. |
| `OODA_STD` | **YES** (prefix `OODA_`) | `oodac_pure_build.sh` L43 can resolve std from that dir |
| `SEED_PUB` | **YES** | substitute pubkey path; body still pinned. Weaker than unsigned skip. |
| `PURE_SKIP_CHECK` / `PURE_NO_ARC` | **YES** | build policy, not inject |
| `OODA` | later exported L70; build uses `env -u OODA` | host soft-pass residual, not this inject |

Minisign is cleaned (`env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin` + abs
`/usr/bin` then `/bin` then `tools/` then PATH fallback).
The **emit host** is not:

    env -u OODA OODAC_BIN="$SEED" "scripts/oodac_pure_build.sh" …

Unsets OODA. Keeps loader gadgets. Keeps `OODA_*`.
`command -v shred` / `srm` run **before** `set -euo` (L16-23)
on attacker PATH.

`.oo` L40-41 is **worse as shell**, **better as env filter**:

    SEED_OODAC=" + seed + " PATH=" + shadow + ":/usr/bin:/bin "
      + root + "/scripts/bootstrap_no_cargo.sh > " + tmpd + "/ci_boot.out"

This is unquoted concat into `process_exec` → `sh -c`.

What the runtime does first (good):

- Drop `BASH_ENV`, `ENV`, `LD_PRELOAD`, `IFS`, parent PATH,
  `TMPDIR`, `HOME`, `SEED_OODAC` (name is not `OODA_`).
- Keep every `OODA_*` / `OO_*`.
- Pin PATH `/usr/bin:/bin`, then the command string may
  prefix another PATH.

What the command string does (bad):

- Writes `SEED_OODAC=` + seed with **no quotes** and **no**
  `sh_arg_ok` at the site.
- Writes redirects to `tmpd + "/ci_boot.out"` with no quotes.
- `OODA_SEED_ALLOW_UNSIGNED` still inherited. Unsigned seed
  still skips minisign.
- `OODA_STD` / `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` / `OODA_FFI_ALLOW_DLOPEN`
  still inherited into the bash child and into pure_build.

`seed` and `tmpd` come from `sh_env_get_or`. Two independent
fails, both live:

1. **No stdout.** `printenv` / `echo` exit 0 → `Ok("")`.
   `.unwrap_or(default)` does not run. `tmpd` is `""`.
   `seed` is `""`.
2. **Even with stdout**, `SEED_OODAC` is not in the child
   env (not `OODA_`). `printenv` fails. `echo DEFAULT`
   returns the default, **never the caller's SEED_OODAC**.
   The .sh honors `SEED_OODAC`. The .oo cannot.

Today, with (1):

    SEED_OODAC= PATH=<shadow>:/usr/bin:/bin ./scripts/bootstrap_no_cargo.sh > /ci_boot.out

- Empty SEED_OODAC → bootstrap falls back to tree seed. Accidental OK.
- Redirect to **`/ci_boot.out`** (and `/ci_fp.out`, `/ci_shadow`).
  Root-fs write if the uid can create it.
- `sh_mkdir_p(p, tmpd)` with `tmpd==""` hits `requires chars_len > 0`
  on a contract-emitting emit, or `mkdir -p` with an empty operand
  if requires are not in that run path.
- bootstrap then sets `TMPDIR=${TMPDIR:-$HOME/.cache/ooda-tmp}`.
  Both TMPDIR and HOME were stripped. HOME expands empty.
  Seed copy lands at **`/.cache/ooda-tmp/bootstrap_seed_oodac`**.

If stdout capture is later fixed and someone feeds a parent
value through (or swaps in `OODA_SEED_OODAC`), `sh_arg_ok`
still allows the inject class:

    SEED_OODAC=x PATH=/tmp/evil /tmp/evil/pwn

Class: letters, space, `=`, `:`, `/`. Concat becomes:

    SEED_OODAC=x PATH=/tmp/evil /tmp/evil/pwn PATH=<shadow>:/usr/bin:/bin <root>/scripts/bootstrap_no_cargo.sh

Prefix assigns `SEED_OODAC` and `PATH`. Command is `/tmp/evil/pwn`.
**That is command injection in the bootstrap invoke.**

Leading space is enough: `SEED_OODAC= /tmp/evil` → empty
assignment, command `/tmp/evil`.

`install_dress_rehearsal.oo` at least calls `dress_gate` /
`sh_arg_ok` before concat. ci_product.oo does not.

Adjacent, not invoked by the twin today:
`bootstrap_no_cargo.oo` interpolates `seed` and `tmpd` into a
large `if [ -z "…"` string (L23) and uses `$(cat seed_path)`
(L33). Switching the twin to the .oo bootstrap would widen
this hunt, not close it.

========================================================================
sh_arg_ok — what it stops here, what it cannot
========================================================================

Landed. Fail-closed on `;|&$` ` () {} <>` quotes backtick
backslash CR LF. Multi-byte UTF-8 is not `char_is_alpha`
(`len==1`). Overlong `;` is 2 bytes → reject. NUL byte is
not in the class → reject. Good against classic meta.

Allowed on purpose, and lethal in **this** file's concat
shape (`VAR=` + user + ` PATH=` + user + ` cmd`):

| Allowed | Why it injects in ci_product.oo |
|---------|----------------------------------|
| space | splits prefix-assign from command |
| `=` | extra assignment (`PATH=…`) |
| `:` | PATH component / URL / TMPDIR split |
| `/` `.` | `../` traversal |
| `-` | option inject |
| `+` `_` | flags / names; not meta |

`sh_arg_ok("")` is **true** (empty loop). Empty is not safe
in an assignment or a redirect.

git / tar / chmod stay shell after the gate. That is DE10 /
`sprint_sec_sh.oot`. Not closed by this wave. Not this file's
job to relitigate, except: ci_product.oo uses `sh_mkdir_p`
and `sh_env_get_or`, so those residuals sit on its setup
path.

ProcessCap is the whole OS. EnvCap is never taken.
`SEED_OODAC` and `TMPDIR` are not `OODA_` keys. EnvCap
`env_get` would deny them. Signature freeze on
`sh_env_get_or(&ProcessCap, …)` is still correct. It is
also why the twin cannot honestly read those keys.

========================================================================
HONESTY HOLES (do not close on paper)
========================================================================

1. **ci_product.oo prints PASSED always** (L47). No fail
   tally. `check` / `expect_*` Results discarded. A failed
   bootstrap still prints PASSED if the process does not exit.
2. **Beat "every listed rail exits 0" is false.** Zero rails
   listed. Zero rails run. `ci_product_rails.oo` absent.
3. **`when`/`and`/`then` are empty** (L17-24). Story, not
   checks. SPRINT already names this. Still true.
4. **L26 hygiene grep is broken.** Literal ` + | grep` after
   `release.sh`. Extra argv `+`. `sh -c` has no `pipefail`.
   `!` on a failing pipeline can PASS the expect.
5. **`.oo` does not honor SEED_OODAC.** printenv cannot see
   it; stdout is empty anyway. Claim in the logline is false.
6. **`.sh` is still the product rail.** GHA step is
   `./scripts/ci_product.sh`. PM same. INT skipped a full
   run this week (long rail / race). Do not say the twin is
   proven.
7. **`within:` is message-only** (scenario.oo residual).
   600s is not a timer. A hung bootstrap is not killed.
8. **`sh_realpath(".")` is slash-fold, not realpath(1).**
   Returns `.`. Fine for this hardcoded input. Do not claim
   cwd resolve.
9. **No live inject probe this turn.** Static only.
   When a rail runner lands, refuse: space in rail, `../`,
   `SEED_OODAC=x PATH=/tmp/e /tmp/e/pwn`, `TMPDIR` with `:`,
   `BASH_ENV` on the .sh, `OODA_SEED_ALLOW_UNSIGNED=1`,
   `/usr/bin/cargo` on the unprefixed .oo PATH.
   Do not PASS on "alnum looks fine."

========================================================================
ATTACK MATRIX
========================================================================

Verdict: BLOCK = refused on the path that exists.
BYPASS = works. OPEN = no runner / no gate yet.
N/A = surface absent.

| # | Attack | .sh | .oo | Sev |
|---|--------|-----|-----|-----|
| R1 | Rail name `; id` as listed literal | BLOCK (quoted) | N/A (no rails) | — |
| R2 | Rail name with space, unquoted concat | N/A (quoted) | **OPEN** if they concat | HIGH |
| R3 | Rail `../evil` | BYPASS if listed | **OPEN** (`sh_arg_ok` allows) | MED |
| R4 | Rails from env / file, no `rail_ok` | N/A today | **OPEN** (file absent) | HIGH |
| P1 | `PATH=evil` before entry; `env` hijack on `#!/usr/bin/env` | **BYPASS** | BLOCK for `process_exec` children (PATH pin) | HIGH on .sh |
| P2 | TMPDIR contains `:` → extra PATH dir | **BYPASS** | same if tmpd used in PATH= | HIGH |
| P3 | `/usr/bin/cargo` while "shadowed" | BLOCK (.sh prepends) | **BYPASS** on unprefixed cmds | MED |
| P4 | Abs-path cargo in a rail | **BYPASS** (log FN) | same | MED |
| P5 | Shadow only cargo/rustc; evil `find`/`grep` | **BYPASS** | pin hides most; prefix reopens | MED |
| E1 | `BASH_ENV` / `ENV` at .sh entry | **BYPASS** | BLOCK (filtered) | CRIT on .sh |
| E2 | `LD_PRELOAD` on seed build | **BYPASS** (minisign only `env -i`) | BLOCK into `sh -c`; **BYPASS** again inside bootstrap.sh once it execs the seed with inherited child env — child of .oo has no LD_*; bootstrap then `env -u OODA` keeps that clean. So E2 is .sh. | HIGH on .sh |
| E3 | `OODA_SEED_ALLOW_UNSIGNED=1` skips minisign | **BYPASS** | **BYPASS** (kept) | HIGH |
| E4 | `OODA_STD` redirects std resolve | **BYPASS** | **BYPASS** | MED |
| E5 | `SEED_OODAC=` + space/`=` concat | BLOCK (quoted assign) | **BYPASS** when seed nonempty; today seed is `""` so dormant | HIGH |
| E6 | Empty tmpd → `> /ci_boot.out` | N/A (bash TMPDIR set) | **BYPASS** today (stdout hole) | HIGH |
| E7 | Empty HOME/TMPDIR → seed at `/.cache/…` | N/A | **BYPASS** today | MED |
| H1 | Twin prints PASSED with no rails | N/A | **BYPASS** (honesty) | CRIT claim |
| H2 | Dropped check Results | N/A | **BYPASS** | HIGH |

========================================================================
RESIDUAL (do not close on paper)
========================================================================

- **Product path is ci_product.sh.** Twin is not a runner.
  `ci_product_rails.oo` absent. 132 rails unported.
- **Rail-name inject is sealed on .sh** by quotes + static
  list. It is **not designed** on .oo. `sh_arg_ok` is the
  wrong class for a leaf name.
- **PATH shadow is a cargo/rustc scarecrow.** .sh keeps
  attacker PATH and `env`. .oo pins `/usr/bin:/bin` and
  then forgets the shadow on fixed_point (and any rail).
  TMPDIR `:` splits PATH on .sh.
- **Bootstrap env is unsanitized on .sh.** `BASH_ENV` and
  `LD_PRELOAD` are live. Minisign is the only `env -i`.
  `OODA_SEED_ALLOW_UNSIGNED` is a kept product-trust skip
  on both paths.
- **.oo bootstrap line is unsanitized concat.** seed/tmpd
  are empty today because exec has no stdout, so the
  spectacular inject is dormant and the root-fs redirect
  is live. Fixing stdout without quoting **activates** E5.
- **sh_arg_ok smoke does not cover this hunt.**
- git/tar/chmod still shell. ProcessCap still reads env.
  No DangerShellCap. Same DE10 residual as `sprint_sec_sh.oot`.

**Not path-A.** Not a CI seal. Next twin must: argv or
`cmd_execute` (not `sh -c` concat); `rail_ok` tighter than
`sh_arg_ok`; PATH=`shadow:/usr/bin:/bin` on **every** child
or drop the shadow story; `env -i` (or the runtime filter
plus an explicit allowlist) around bootstrap; refuse
`OODA_SEED_ALLOW_UNSIGNED` on the product rail; fail the
script when a check is Err; stop printing PASSED if the
rails did not run.

Static only. No inject probe this turn.
